# 渴了么 (KeLeME) — Project Rules

> Project-specific decisions and constraints. For architecture details see `CLAUDE.md`.
> For Dart style see `.cursor/rules/dart-style.mdc`.

## Architecture Decisions

- **State management**: `ChangeNotifier` with manual `addListener` — no Provider/BLoC/Riverpod packages. Keep it simple.
- **Dependency injection**: Constructor injection. Pass `UserProvider` (and other providers) explicitly — no GetIt or service locators.
- **Routing**: `MaterialApp.routes` with named routes. No GoRouter or auto_route.
- **Data persistence**: `SharedPreferences` for user profile/daily data, `Hive` for structured collections (memory facts, session summaries, custom reminders).
- **Networking**: `dio` for HTTP requests. AI backend calls go through `AiService`.
- **Error handling**: `try-catch` with `debugPrint`. No `Either`/`dartz`.

## Directory Structure

```
lib/
  core/           # Shared across features
    models/       # UserProfile, DrinkLog, WeatherData, etc.
    providers/    # UserProvider (app-wide state)
    services/     # NotificationService, WeatherService, etc.
    theme/        # AppTheme, AppColors
    utils/        # GoalPredictor, helpers
  features/       # Feature modules
    <feature>/
      models/     # Feature-specific models
      providers/  # Feature-specific ChangeNotifiers
      screens/    # Full-page widgets
      services/   # Feature-specific services
      widgets/    # Reusable UI components
  common/
    widgets/      # Cross-feature widgets (GlassCard, ProgressRing)
```

Do NOT introduce `data/domain/presentation` layers or `usecases/repositories` abstractions.

## Widget Rules

- Use `const` constructors wherever possible.
- Use `ValueKey` or `ObjectKey` when widgets reorder in lists.
- Keep `build()` short — extract `_buildXxx()` helper methods for sections.
- Always `dispose()` controllers: `AnimationController`, `TextEditingController`, `ScrollController`, `StreamSubscription`.
- Wrap unstable subtrees with `ErrorWidget.builder` or a custom error boundary widget to prevent full-screen crashes.
- Use `RepaintBoundary` around expensive custom paint widgets (e.g., `ProgressRing`).

## Performance

- Use `ListView.builder` / `GridView.builder` for dynamic lists — never `Column(children: list.map(...))` for unbounded data.
- Minimize `setState` scope — only call it on the smallest `StatefulWidget` that needs to rebuild.
- Avoid `Opacity` widget for hiding; prefer `Visibility` or conditional rendering.
- Cache network images with `CachedNetworkImage` if image loading is added.
- Build release APKs with `--split-per-abi` to reduce size.

## Testing

- Mirror `lib/` structure in `test/` (e.g., `test/core/providers/user_provider_test.dart`).
- Unit test `UserProvider` and `ChatProvider` business logic with mocked `SharedPreferences`.
- Widget test screens with `pumpWidget` and verify key interactions.
- Use `mockito` for mocking services; avoid over-mocking — test real logic, mock only I/O boundaries.
- Name tests descriptively: `'addDrink increases todayMl and appends to logs'`.

## Anti-patterns to Avoid

- Putting business logic (calculations, persistence, API calls) inside widget `build()` methods.
- Deeply nesting widgets (>5 levels) — extract into named widgets or helper methods.
- Hardcoding colors/sizes — use `AppColors`, `AppTheme`, and theme constants.
- Forgetting to check `mounted` before calling `setState` after async operations.
- Creating new object instances inside `build()` that could be `const` or cached.
